./specs/021-strata-inference-research/benchmarks.md:22:The checked-in `fixtures/benchmark_prompts.json` contains the exact rendered prompts and token IDs for 4,096, 32,768, and 65,536 tokens, plus per-prompt little-endian token-ID SHA-256, vocabulary/stop-ID assertions, and construction provenance. It is generated with the Nix-pinned tokenizer/template by `nix develop --command cargo run -p agentix-qwen --example build_benchmark_prompt_fixtures`; `cargo test -p agentix-qwen --test benchmark_prompts` re-renders each prompt and verifies its token IDs and hash. The deterministic fixture explicitly records its repeated text segment and padding suffix, so prompt construction does not silently repeat text. Fixture file SHA-256: `c5a255bd4a271c3a14eebc762617dc511757dfa55b2019482d0d0075f021c939`. Cold means a fresh worker process and empty OS page cache where the operator can safely arrange it; if page-cache control is unavailable, record the limitation and call the run process-cold only. Warm means one unmeasured priming request followed by the measured request in the same loaded worker. Three measured repetitions are reported individually, with median and min/max; no outlier is discarded.
