./specs/021-strata-inference-research/contracts.md:1:# Qwen backend integration contracts
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/contracts.md:9:Keep the existing worktree base; do not merge sibling branches implicitly. Model computation belongs in the network-free `agentix-qwen` library. Put generated/unsafe GGML and GGUF calls behind `agentix-qwen-sys`. Run the CUDA-linked Qwen engine in an `agentix-qwen-worker` process separate from `agentix-llama`, using the daemon's existing Unix-socket HTTP/SSE proxy boundary. Neither the generic inference crate nor router may depend on CUDA/native code through this backend.
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/contracts.md:11:The daemon uses Unix-socket worker proxying and does not link `agentix-infer` directly. `AGENTIX_QWEN_SOCKET` defaults to `/run/agentix/qwen.sock`, and `AGENTIX_QWEN_MODEL` selects one exact identifier (default `qwen3.8-flash-next`). The gateway now routes exact chat-completion matches to the Qwen socket and returns an explicit service-unavailable error without falling back to llama/cloud. Unsupported embeddings, responses, and Anthropic-message requests for the exact Qwen ID fail explicitly. Existing llama selection and socket remain unchanged. The worker validates pinned shard hashes, config geometry and tokenizer vocabulary before binding its local socket; it exposes health, model-list, greedy text completion and bounded SSE text streams. Tools, reasoning-channel output, non-greedy sampling, embeddings and multimodal input are rejected. No endpoint may start or depend on Strata.
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:15:| Original Qwen MTP tensors | `de4b8e4d43b917e7706784d8bb445c9af86a3540` | `tools/mtp_fetch.py::PINNED_REVISION`, per-tensor SHA256 table |
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:16:| Qwen tokenizer | `de4b8e4d43b917e7706784d8bb445c9af86a3540` | `tokenizer.json`, pinned Nix hash `sha256-CZf0EMV6H05TsJ5L6PShctkO3ZVkNo+whHAwk3IpufM=`; addressable token count 248,077 |
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:17:| Qwen chat template | `de4b8e4d43b917e7706784d8bb445c9af86a3540` | `chat_template.jinja`, pinned Nix hash `sha256-w8+eNKv0+eNsLXIWWqnBMtPipyW2wlhqqjqK+deoEEE=`; three rendering fixtures pass with the MiniJinja compatibility callback |
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:18:| Qwen safetensors index | `de4b8e4d43b917e7706784d8bb445c9af86a3540` | Captured `model.safetensors.index.json` SHA256 `99e815241ef03325536b0aaa4441deea45174c17fae31e10f0bb456410c590de`; all 1,658 index name/shard assignments exactly match header-only reads across all 131 shards. Beyond the separately described PLE row, only small rank-one norm, `A_log`, and `dt_bias` payload samples have been fetched; no bulk payload was downloaded. |
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:19:| Qwen text source tensor headers | Same pinned Qwen revision | Range-read the 8-byte length prefix and complete SafeTensors JSON header (about 225 KiB total) from each of the 131 shards; no tensor payload was downloaded in this step. `evidence/qwen3_8_flash_next_text_tensor_headers.tsv` joins all 1,294 text checkpoint names to Agentix's source-to-GGUF mapping and records dtype, source shape, shard, and shard-local data offsets (SHA256 `53eaab9924d0626f1cf4f85de21f3709ccb4c21764cb33ac37618d70b5720a39`). The text tensors are 1,291 BF16 and three I64 PLE metadata vectors. Across all 1,658 header entries (including vision/MTP), every dtype/shape matches its declared byte range and all per-shard ranges are contiguous. `pinned_source_header_geometry_maps_to_complete_gguf_schema` checks every text source mapping/transform and proves its declared source geometry yields the complete 1,224-target GGUF schema geometry, including split, squeeze, and concatenated PLE shapes. Payload values remain unverified except for the specific PLE row and the direct norm/`A_log` vectors recorded separately. |
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:20:| Qwen norm and GatedDeltaNet source vector samples | Same pinned Qwen revision | Range-read a full 128-value BF16 linear-attention norm vector and 48-value BF16 layer-0 `A_log` and `dt_bias` vectors, plus their published F32 GGUF counterparts. The norm and `dt_bias` values match exactly after their direct transforms. The A-log values match within `1e-6` relative tolerance after `-exp` and head reorder. Offsets, hashes, limits and sample scope are recorded in `evidence/qwen3_8_flash_next_norm_vector_parity.json`, `evidence/qwen3_8_flash_next_alog_vector_parity.json`, and `evidence/qwen3_8_flash_next_dt_bias_vector_parity.json`. Tests wrap only these captured samples; no complete tensor payload was downloaded. |
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:22:| Qwen text source-to-GGUF name map | Same pinned Qwen and llama.cpp revisions | Agentix maps all 1,294 text-side index entries to metadata or GGUF names. The 1,224 unique targets equal the pinned Qwen schema and published shard header. Crosswalk: `evidence/qwen3_8_flash_next_source_to_gguf.tsv`, SHA256 `6ff72f51f99488cb2cfa7f7f7a1d7ede6841480cbeef3287ceb09dc8020ce7e0` (source tensor mapping list). It records PLE shard concatenation, indexer Q/K split, expert gate/up split, PLE norm offset/convolution squeeze, and GatedDeltaNet value-head reorder. The header-geometry integration test reconciles source dimensions for all text tensors with all target schema extents after those transforms. One norm and one A_log vector now have published-target value comparisons; most transformed payload values, quantized payloads and model loading remain unverified/unimplemented. Vision and MTP (364 index entries) are outside the text-only target. |
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:23:| Qwen PLE safetensors shard headers | Same pinned Qwen revision | Range-read the 8-byte prefix and complete JSON header for each of the 33 source shards containing PLE tensors. All 128 PLE tensors are BF16 `[2500012,160]`, yielding 320,001,536 rows of width 160 and 102,400,491,520 logical source bytes total. Evidence TSV: `evidence/qwen3_8_flash_next_ple_shard_headers.tsv`, SHA256 `d108021214b61a9fed86defb2bf25e963f3a03660f8856ab6eff351a4c9a3355`. These shapes and total rows match the published GGUF PLE extents `[160,320001536]` after GGUF dimension reversal. One row from `shard_0` is compared to published GGUF row 0 below. |
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:24:| Qwen source-to-published-GGUF PLE row parity | Same pinned Qwen revision and ggml-org GGUF revision `052beeaca7bec4a303e59cc7bc630c4f3a1b845d` | Range-read source BF16 row 0 (320 bytes, SHA256 `67354d4be4c2d2d8ed2f6003c5e98e56015072f08bbd5f62c6b38589628a35cb`) and GGUF Q4_0 row 0 (90 bytes, SHA256 `34098719c5d2b94c40150f2fbf5e04859571d27a1df605134e8deadb0d01cf73`). The new SafeTensors row reader obtains the source values; dequantized GGUF values match within max absolute error `0.003`. Evidence and exact limitations: `evidence/qwen3_8_flash_next_ple_row_parity.json`. This is one-row parity only. |
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:25:| Qwen non-PLE norm vector parity | Same pinned Qwen and ggml-org GGUF revisions above | Range-read the complete 256-byte BF16 source vector at source-file bytes `[110836296,110836551]` (tensor `model.language_model.layers.0.linear_attn.norm.weight`) and its 512-byte F32 target at GGUF-file bytes `[55842688,55843199]` (`blk.0.ssm_norm.weight`). Agentix's bounded SafeTensors vector reader and direct source transform match all 128 values exactly through the GGUF dense-row reader. Payload sample SHA256 values, tensor offsets, and the synthetic-reader test's scope are recorded in `evidence/qwen3_8_flash_next_norm_vector_parity.json`; the raw bytes are checked in beside it. This is one vector and does not verify complete shard payloads. |
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:26:| Qwen config | `de4b8e4d43b917e7706784d8bb445c9af86a3540` | `config.json` SHA256 `889658f2508e8c61d409b02e70e0d78d8d4452ec65aaafbe129805d213d2e74b`; independently matches bytes fetched from the immutable Hugging Face revision and is checked by the parser fixture |
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:27:| Transformers Qwen4-Exp reference | `2fa1fdd5b27ae54bdcee0516848c7963393a5f5c` | Captured `modeling_qwen4_exp.py` SHA256 `f94401c10c1bbafd814cc174ba6f40dde1f40b35715ce1ae827ccf8ee3cd81fa`, `configuration_qwen4_exp.py` SHA256 `ac0950ab34516d26fe4f6b28cffe0649d763449effe44e42b5913463806f7e0b`; both hashes independently match the raw files fetched from this exact GitHub commit. |
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:28:| Qwen4-Exp PLE source/index comparison | Same pinned Qwen revision | `modeling_qwen4_exp.py` constructs one dense embedding parameter; the index instead lists 128 `model.language_model.layers.1.ple.ple_embedding.ngram_embedding.shard_i.weight` keys (i=0..127). Header-only reads show all 128 are BF16 `[2500012,160]` with contiguous file ranges and numeric shard names; the pinned llama.cpp converter concatenates them in numeric order. Their 320,001,536 rows match the padded GGUF table and contain 90 rows beyond the 320,001,446 hash-addressable rows. `agentix-qwen` now opens these indexed source shards as bounded BF16 row readers and composes them in numeric order; a synthetic public-opener test covers geometry and cross-shard dispatch. One actual source row matches its published quantized GGUF counterpart within 0.003. Full shard payload acquisition, broader value parity, and model-wide tensor loading remain open. |
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:30:| GGML quantized CUDA/CPU paths | bundled with `llama-cpp-sys-2` 0.1.154 above | Inspected `ggml-common.h` block definitions, `ggml.c` type traits, `ggml-quants.c` CPU dequantizers, and CUDA `dequantize.cuh`, `mmq.cu`, `mmvq.cu`. IQ2_XS: 74 bytes/256 values; IQ3_S: 110 bytes/256 values. `agentix-qwen-sys::QuantizedRows` now decodes IQ2_XS/IQ3_S rows through the pinned GGML CPU `to_float` callbacks; row bounds, block geometry, finite output, and GGUF tensor extent are checked. Synthetic row tests exercise both encodings, but no hash-verified published IQ2_XS/IQ3_S weight row has been compared yet. IQ4_NL decoding matches the callback for synthetic bytes and one sampled real row; Q4_0 has synthetic byte-layout tests and one sampled real row. CUDA kernel/device parity remains unimplemented. GGML quantization metadata says IQ2_XS requires an importance matrix; IQ3_S does not. |
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:31:| llama.cpp Qwen4-Exp converter | Tag `b10660`, commit `6c84c7d5d8833c6e0df69628f75a0f599797934e` | Official merged PR #27742 adds Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (`qwen4exp`) conversion/inference support. Pinned `conversion/qwen4exp.py` sorts PLE shard indices numerically, checks a shared final row dimension, and concatenates chunks into `per_layer_token_embd.weight`. It also records architecture metadata and converts the fused indexer Q/K projection. This is independent conversion evidence only; it is not an Agentix dependency or implementation source. |
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:32:| llama.cpp shared Qwen converter behavior | Same pinned llama.cpp commit | `conversion/qwen.py` splits aggregated `mlp.experts.gate_up_proj` into gate/up tensors and specifies GatedDeltaNet's grouped-to-tiled V-axis permutations; `conversion/base.py` writes separate expert gate/up tensors. The pinned implementation keeps Q/K rows and convolution channels in place, reorders only QKV's V rows, reorders Z/alpha/beta/dt-bias rows, transforms A-log with `-exp` before its value-head reorder, and reorders output-projection columns. Agentix's `source::transform_qwen4exp_f32_tensor` dispatches these layouts and the indexer/expert/norm/PLE-convolution transforms through checked CPU primitives; captured A-log and dt-bias vectors match their published transformed tensors within their recorded tolerances. Source F32/F16/BF16 rank-two tensors now have bounded, finite F32 row decoding; PLE hash arrays have a typed reader and tested GGUF UINT64 metadata rewriter. Complete source tensor mapping/loading/parity, PLE shard assembly and model-wide serialization remain open. |
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:33:| Published Qwen3.8-Flash-Next GGUF PLE tensor | `ggml-org/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF`, revision `052beeaca7bec4a303e59cc7bc630c4f3a1b845d` | Read only the first 16 MiB of the 102,037,973,504-byte second IQ4_NL shard into a sparse local file, then parsed its GGUF header with the pinned Agentix inspector. `per_layer_token_embd.weight` is GGML `q4_0`, shape `[160, 320001536]`, payload 28,800,138,240 bytes. The file's LFS SHA256 is `0299b147e42517ff8fa3a4fa66d370c77ce01c44ed8cbc3451b7a42caad5fc10`. Also read exactly the first 90-byte PLE row at file offset 3,015,862,016; Agentix decoded 160 finite values. Header and sample-row evidence are captured in `evidence/ggml-qwen-ple-header.json`; the remainder of the weight payload was not downloaded or verified. |
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:34:| Published Qwen3.8-Flash-Next IQ3_S candidate PLE row | `ISTA-DASLab/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GSQ-RCO-GGUF`, revision `ed59f92082b1e93c0e96d60a8b11aab089b52f09` | The full split-2 payload is acquired and its SHA256 matches the publisher manifest. Row 0 at offset 192 has SHA256 `4b067ea426d9767a81185b36042c6612de8a5f41fca76b97feb4bc5b8298f1ab`; all 160 Agentix IQ4_NL values match the pinned GGML type-traits dequantizer within `1e-7`. The exact bytes are embedded in the native parity test; metadata and parity scope are recorded in `evidence/iq3s-ple-iq4nl-sample.json`. This does not validate full-model operator outputs.
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:36:| Published IQ4_NL GGUF split set | Same repository/revision as above; both `Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-IQ4_NL-0000*-of-00002.gguf` shards | Downloaded all 10,945,440 bytes of shard 1; SHA256 `851652eef30d117a34fdc0d13e05da4c488a8cdad3654d38c4aa69a2d8a1fabc` matches the pinned publisher hash. Agentix reports GGUF v3, architecture `qwen4exp`, split 0/2, zero tensors, data offset 10,945,432. Combined this full file with only shard 2's first 16 MiB in a sparse file; `inspect_gguf_set` validated sequential split indices, split count 2, unique names, and 1,224 total tensors. Evidence is in `evidence/ggml-qwen-iq4nl-shards.json`. This validates the header directory set, not shard-2 payload integrity. |
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:37:| Pinned llama.cpp Qwen4-Exp tensor schema | `ggml-org/llama.cpp` commit `6c84c7d5d8833c6e0df69628f75a0f599797934e` | `src/models/qwen4exp.cpp` declares GGUF tensor names and shapes used by the Agentix-owned `schema` module. Agentix validates all 1,224 names/extents from the published IQ4_NL split header against the pinned config with no missing, unexpected, duplicate, or mismatched tensors. Shard 2 omits architecture metadata; set validation obtains `qwen4exp` from shard 1. This is GGUF geometry validation only, not source safetensors mapping or weight loading. |
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:38:| Published IQ4_NL GGUF shard-2 tensor inventory | Same repository/revision as above; `Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-IQ4_NL-00002-of-00002.gguf` | Metadata-only parser inventory from the same 16 MiB header range: 1,224 tensors, split index 1 of 2. Types: 24 BF16, 1 F16, 388 F32, 292 IQ4_NL, 1 Q4_0 (PLE), 518 Q8_0. The 1,224-row TSV `evidence/ggml-qwen-iq4nl-shard-2-tensors.tsv` is SHA256-pinned in the companion JSON. Agentix now has bounded row reads for all six observed storage types; this inventory still does not establish source-to-GGUF tensor mapping or payload correctness. |
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:39:| Reduced Qwen4-Exp architecture-fixture candidate | [ji-farthing/RalphQwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF](https://huggingface.co/ji-farthing/RalphQwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF), mutable model-card page inspected 2026-10-13 | The card describes random initialization and training on synthetic data, reduced geometry (4 layers, width 320), a 783 MB F32 GGUF, and conversion with llama.cpp `f8dbcd6`; it says upstream loading was untested. Not selected as acceptance coverage: it is not original Qwen checkpoint data, is not a small pinned test artifact, and does not establish compatibility with Agentix's pinned upstream revision. It may be reconsidered only as a separately labeled external smoke fixture after immutable file/revision verification and a locally reviewed size/dependency plan. |
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:40:| GGML Q4_0 storage and kernels | bundled with `llama-cpp-sys-2` 0.1.154 above | Q4_0 uses 32 values per 18-byte block. Five blocks encode one 160-value PLE row (90 bytes); GGML's checked tensor byte size matches the captured tensor header exactly. Agentix's isolated Q4_0 row decoder passes synthetic layout/malformed-input checks and matches the pinned native CPU dequantizer for the first hash-verified PLE row within `1e-7`. Target-GPU execution remains open; this does not imply Qwen4-Exp model-loader support in the crate. |
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:42:The separate pinned IQ3_S candidate at `ISTA-DASLab/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GSQ-RCO-GGUF`, revision `ed59f92082b1e93c0e96d60a8b11aab089b52f09`, stores its second-shard PLE tensor as IQ4_NL with the same `[160,320001536]` extents and 90-byte rows. Its GGUF data offset is 192, unlike the ggml-org preset's offset. The first 90-byte row was range-read at file offset 192 (SHA256 `4b067ea426d9767a81185b36042c6612de8a5f41fca76b97feb4bc5b8298f1ab`) and decoded to finite values. Full metadata and limitations are in [the IQ3_S sample evidence](evidence/iq3s-ple-iq4nl-sample.json). This IQ4_NL evidence applies to this candidate; it does not change the separate ggml-org preset's Q4_0 tensor type.
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:59:The native binding dependency is already present transitively for `agentix-llama`; the selected design calls only GGML/GGUF APIs from a separate Qwen worker process. No Strata package, source tree, generated pack, or helper is in this dependency path. A feature-level `cargo tree` audit and binary/package review remain required after the sys crate is added.
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:61:The installed baseline catalog reports Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct-Q4_K_M at 18,556,689,568 bytes. Its installed digest and source revision still need host verification.
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:65:Strata's root LICENSE and its vendored ggml notice are MIT. These are historical research observations: user direction excludes reuse of Strata code regardless of license. Source any general-purpose compute dependency independently and preserve its own attribution. Model-hub metadata for the selected ISTA snapshots reports Apache-2.0, while the upstream Qwen model card reports a Qwen community license. Do not treat either metadata label as resolving the full derivative-weight licensing chain; preserve model provenance and review the actual applicable license files before redistribution. Local research does not settle redistribution terms.
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:73:Official upstream references: [merged Qwen4-Exp support PR #27742](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/27742), [converter at pinned commit](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/blob/6c84c7d5d8833c6e0df69628f75a0f599797934e/conversion/qwen4exp.py), [published GGUF model card](https://huggingface.co/ggml-org/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF), [published first IQ4_NL shard at the inspected revision](https://huggingface.co/ggml-org/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF/blob/052beeaca7bec4a303e59cc7bc630c4f3a1b845d/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-IQ4_NL-00001-of-00002.gguf), and [published second IQ4_NL shard at the inspected revision](https://huggingface.co/ggml-org/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GGUF/blob/052beeaca7bec4a303e59cc7bc630c4f3a1b845d/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-IQ4_NL-00002-of-00002.gguf).
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:75:| IQ3_S candidate complete inventory and payload | `ISTA-DASLab/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GSQ-RCO-GGUF`, revision `ed59f92082b1e93c0e96d60a8b11aab089b52f09` | Both complete shards now match their publisher SHA256 values. The full inventories contain 1,223 tensors in split 1 and one PLE tensor in split 2; all 1,224 names/extents match the pinned Qwen schema. Type counts are BF16 484, F16 1, F32 292, IQ2_S 40, IQ3_S 20, IQ3_XXS 34, IQ4_NL 87, IQ4_XS 45, Q2_0 9, Q4_K 47, Q5_K 35, Q6_K 129, Q8_0 1. Full inventory TSV hashes remain `3d426fabc3e15f081c9f29ce835ce49c86033cc3ae766dfc23112ed2fb21985e` (split 1) and `2b1374d06940668d6d5f458c05f6f928afc6606453cb77cf8c8b4b455070e52f` (split 2). `evidence/ista_iq3s_full_payload_sample_rows.tsv` records one finite decoded row for each of the 13 storage types. These checks establish file integrity, header schema and sampled decoder operation; not full tensor numeric parity, CUDA behavior or model inference.
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/sources.md:77:Follow-up acquisition 2026-10-13: both full payloads were downloaded to `/home/sam/home/agentix/.cache/agentix-qwen/iq3s-ed59f92082b1e93c0e96d60a8b11aab089b52f09/`; exact manifest sizes and publisher SHA256 values match for both splits (split 1 `4c1eb2ceb4915e1192f4f386021897bde56a97f40a0bb78bb86465e0f7d2aca3`; split 2 `316b46f3a2dbd68c900f43136ab9449f9dcc3725dfd8c794847c204bc161e113`). The complete split set passes Agentix's Qwen schema validator: 1,224/1,224 tensor names/extents, no missing, extra, duplicate, shape-mismatched or unsupported tensors. The bounded dense/quantized row validator decoded one row from each of all 13 candidate storage types; every sampled value was finite. Durable TSV sample evidence is `evidence/ista_iq3s_full_payload_sample_rows.tsv`. The actual split-2 PLE row 0 at offset 192 hashes to `4b067ea426d9767a81185b36042c6612de8a5f41fca76b97feb4bc5b8298f1ab` and matches the earlier range capture. This validates file identity, header schema and one row per storage type; it is not full-tensor parity or model inference.
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/tasks.md:1:# Tasks: Agentix-owned Qwen Flash Next inference
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/tasks.md:3:**Scope**: Updated research, independent design, staged implementation and verification. CPU reference/storage/tokenizer/identity foundations, schema-validated GGUF row access, a reusable stateful 48-block CPU decoder, an isolated Unix-socket Qwen worker, and exact-model daemon chat routing are implemented. Worker lifecycle, capability breadth, independent model parity, CUDA execution and target-host acceptance remain open.
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/tasks.md:9:- [x] T002 Revise `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `decision.md` and checklist for Qwen with no Strata code reuse.
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/tasks.md:13:- [ ] T006 [US1] Pin original Qwen reference/configuration/tokenizer/template and quantization definitions; write complete operator/state/tensor contract in `qwen-design.md` and provenance in `sources.md` (depends T003). Partial: pinned converter evidence establishes numeric PLE shard concatenation and common row width; the ggml-org IQ4_NL preset has Q4_0 PLE `[160,320001536]`, while the separate IQ3_S candidate has IQ4_NL PLE with the same extents. The full two-shard IQ3_S candidate now matches both publisher SHA256 values and passes schema validation for all 1,224 tensors. All 1,294 text checkpoint names map to 1,224 GGUF targets; all 128 source PLE headers verify BF16 `[2500012,160]` rows, totaling 320,001,536 physical rows, 90 beyond the 320,001,446 logical n-gram rows. Sampled Q4_0 and IQ4_NL rows match pinned GGML dequantization within `1e-7`; one source BF16 PLE row matches published Q4_0 within `0.003`. Actual candidate decoding covers all 13 observed storage types, and the artifact sampler now runs one token through all 48 blocks and emits finite logits. Remaining source-value coverage, independent full-model output parity, and target-device correctness remain open.
./specs/021-strata-inference-research/tasks.md:14:- [ ] T007 [US3] Select independent loader/compute dependencies and Ampere/Nix strategy; document supported formats, provenance and no-Strata dependency audit in `qwen-design.md` (depends T006). Partial: pinned llama.cpp converter confirms upstream architecture support exists; `llama-cpp-sys-2` 0.1.154 provides generic GGUF primitives but no Qwen4-Exp model loader. Pinned `safetensors` 0.8.0 metadata deserialization now validates source headers and a bounded BF16 file-row reader feeds the pure PLE interface. Exact normal dependency trees in `quickstart.md` confirm that `agentix-qwen` has no native GGML/GGUF dependency and neither Qwen tree includes Strata; the native sys crate owns GGUF parsing and row decoding. GGUF bounded row decoding covers all 13 types in the inspected IQ3_S candidate and 15 types across the inspected artifacts; quantized and F16/BF16 readers are checked against native GGML conversion callbacks, and Q4_0/IQ4_NL also match one hash-verified published row each. One real IQ3_S expert row from the pinned candidate was decoded through the bounded rank-three reader; no independent numeric oracle comparison exists. A CUDA matvec probe and an ignored device-parity test are implemented but cannot execute in this environment because `libcuda.so.1` and NVIDIA device nodes are absent. The sys Nix package builds with its CUDA feature, but full-model tensor mapping/loading, CUDA kernels and target-device execution remain open.
